      "title": "Letterboxd review of Gladiator",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Gladiator\"] I could tell you Gladiator is a surprisingly restrained boxing picture from Rowdy “Roadhouse” Harrington, featuring great performances from Ossie Davis, Brian Dennehy (in full God mode), and James Marshall. I could tell you Gladiator explores the economic divide between the haves and the have nots, shining a light on how the have nots are mercilessly exploited by the haves. I could tell you Gladiator is a fun boxing underdog story in the tradition of Rocky. Or I could tell you the fight scenes are cinematic as fuck -- total and complete slobberknockers – including one that takes place in a vio",
