      "title": "Letterboxd review of Gladiator",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Gladiator\"] The “other” Gladiator. Rewatched this after decades of my last viewing. Loved this movie when I was 12 years old, and honestly, it holds up well. Two Chicago teens get trapped in the dangerous underworld of illegal, bare-knuckle boxing. James Marshall & Cuba Gooding Jr rock their roles. They’re exploited by a ruthless, corrupt fight promoter played by Brian Dennehy—Dennehy always crushes these scumbag roles. Robert Loggia also pops up in the film—one of those solid-as-a-rock character actors you’re always happy to see. Fun forgotten movie from 1992. Directed by Rowdy Herrington—the total mens",
